A||||5||msweldon||What are the differences between the Fiero Getrags and Beretta/Cavalier Getrags?||||1||
Z||000000||msweldon||12-11-2000||04:28 PM||||What are the differences between the Fiero Getrags and Beretta/Cavalier Getrags besides what can be changed with Rodney Dickmans kit?<P>I guess I should ask what are all of the versions of the 282 5spd Tranny?<P>thanks,<BR>marc||||reg||1
Z||000001||fiero56||12-11-2000||04:31 PM||||Not much. FDs I suppose, not much else though.||||reg||1
Z||000002||pherder||12-11-2000||06:16 PM||||Lots ...<P>If it is from a V6 then the gear ratios and the FDR is the same as the Fiero's Getrag.<P>If it is from a Quad 4 ... it will NOT fit the Fiero engines (it also has different gear ratios and a could have a 3.94(?):1 FDR if it was from a Olds Achieva SCX).<P>The shifting rod that comes out of the transaxle that the shifter mechnism attaches to is 11 MM shorter on the FWD transaxles thus requiring Rodney's kit to be able to shift into 1/2 and 5/R all the way.<P>The later model Getrags have either an internal hydraulic throwout bearing (and the Fiero's master cylinder will NOT push enough fluid to make it work) OR it will have an external slave that bolts directly to the bell housing unlike the Fiero's slave that bolts to a bracket.  <P>Rodney has the parts to convert the external slave to be replaced with an adapter for the Fiero's Getrag slave (I have use one on my FWD transaxle install).<P>One other problem with the FWD Getrags ... at one point they redesigned the housing and did away with the mounting bosses that the Fiero uses to mount brackets to for the mounts.   I have one of those Getrags and haven't decided how I want to mount it in a Fiero ... yet.<P>Paul<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||msweldon||12-12-2000||11:10 AM||||Thanks for the Info!!!<P>Moreover, could you tell me which FWD Getrags e.g. Cars, Year  work well swapping into our fieros?<P>Thanks,<BR>marc||||reg||1
Z||000004||bHooper||12-12-2000||11:36 AM||||the Getrag in my car came out of a '87 Corsica!<P>serve's me right... i hate those cars so damn much!<P>anyway, you will also need to change the speedo gear and the inner shaft seal, to be safe.<P>i am very pleased with mine, it feels just like the one that was in my GT since birth!<P>of course, it is the same  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000005||pherder||12-12-2000||06:22 PM||||DOH!!!  Forgot ALL about the VSS differences ...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><P>I believe Rodney has the info on what years will work, either on his site or email him.  I believe you will find the info on his Getrag info area.<P>Paul||||reg||11
